<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boleslaus II of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/999">999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Boleslaus the Pious, Boleslav II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boleslaus II, called the Pious, was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from 967 or 972 until 999. He founded the bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> in 973 and in 995 massacred the rival Slavník family, completing Přemyslid control of Bohemia. Late in his reign he lost Silesia and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> region to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boleslaus-ii-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Boleslaus II of Bohemia" width="100" height="150" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous fresco in Znojmo (CZ) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boles%C5%82aw_II_Pobo%C5%BCny.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
